# The desktop wallpaper package's source list (Assets/cubit-wallpapers/):
# the one place a wallpaper is declared. One Wallpaper_Sources
# (CCL.Interfaces.Wallpapers.SOURCES_TYPE_SOURCE), checked by the type
# system. tools/build_wallpaper_assets.py writes each picture as
# <name>.qoi, reduced to width x height, and the package's catalog.ccl, which
# the desktop reads at run time: adding or removing a picture is an edit
# here, not a code change. The first entry is the default wallpaper.
(Wallpaper_Sources images => [
  (Wallpaper_Source
    name => "cubes"
    label => "Cubes"
    source => "wallpaper2.png"
    width => 2048
    height => 576
    attribution => "CuBit project owner's original wallpaper2.png (5120x1440); redistribution terms to be confirmed before a public release")])
